2.2 Optional legacy workflow: stepwise selection
If the source workflow remains:

label it as a legacy or demonstration approach;
explain that repeated data-driven selection can make p-values and confidence intervals overly optimistic;
do not say that stepwise selection controls overfitting;
compare the selected model with the prespecified model.

The source selected age and fasting blood sugar, with adjusted \(R^2\) approximately 0.119:
\[\widehat{SBP}=103.3+0.52(\mathrm{age})+9.09(\mathrm{FBS&gt;120})\]
Recalculate this in jamovi and verify the coding of fbs.

1.2 Learning outcomes
By the end of the workshop, participants should be able to:

distinguish correlation from regression;
choose Pearson’s or Spearman’s correlation;
fit and interpret simple and multiple linear regression models in jamovi;
interpret coefficients, confidence intervals, p-values, \(R^2\) and adjusted \(R^2\);
assess linearity, residual normality, homoscedasticity, influential observations and multicollinearity;
explain the effect of transforming an outcome variable;
save a jamovi analysis so that data, settings and output remain together.
